# Skyline Scoreboard — Claude Code instructions

## Purpose
Build and maintain Skyline Church's executive attendance dashboard for Pastor Joe Ross. Keep the existing responsive design, filters, historical comparisons, reporting notes and print view. Numbers represent recorded participation, not unique people.

## Commands
Use Node.js 20+.
- npm run check
- npm run build
- npm run preview (Python 3, static fallback snapshot only)

The app has no third-party runtime dependencies. Plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript assets are embedded into a Cloudflare Worker by scripts/build.mjs. public/core.js contains calculations; public/app.js renders the UI.

## Data rules
- All-campus recorded in-person attendance excludes online but includes mid-week ministry participation already present in source campus totals.
- Weekend worship attendance requires separately verified service data. Do not infer it from the monthly aggregate.
- Monthly average = recorded monthly total / completed Sunday-ending reporting weeks.
- YoY = current weekly average / same-month prior-year weekly average - 1.
- Missing or zero prior-year denominator: N/A.
- Green >=10%; yellow >-4% and <10%; red <=-4%, using unrounded rates.
- Partial-month comparisons use prior-year full-month weekly average and must disclose that limitation.
- Headline YoY uses completed months. YTD attendance averages include all completed reporting weeks.
- Never add youth subservice counts on top of campus totals.
- Preserve historical attendance, nulls and recorded zeros. A missing row does not establish a campus closure.
- Source totals must reconcile: physical + online = reported.
- Do not infer retention, invite culture, spiritual outcomes or leader effectiveness from attendance alone.
- Preserve reporting notes until the source owner resolves them.

