# Skyline weekly attendance refresh

Preserve this Site’s existing audience. The data updater requires the owner's existing Site service credential in a dedicated X-Skyline-Update-Authorization: Bearer header. The server verifies its SHA-256 hash against a protected runtime value; the raw credential is never stored in source or served to the browser. This protection remains in place when the dashboard is public or shared.

## Weekly source and write path

1. Get this Site with Sites tools; verify it is published, active and owned by the task's user. Obtain its existing service credential from get_site. Do not generate, rotate, store, print or put that credential in an automation prompt. Send it only to this Site origin, in OAI-Sites-Authorization: Bearer and X-Skyline-Update-Authorization: Bearer headers. The latter is required for writes even when the site is public. If the service token has changed and writes return 403, stop and report the credential mismatch; do not silently replace authorization or weaken access rules.
2. Independently use the owner’s Gmail connector to locate the newest email from sflores@skylinechurch.org with subject Attendance Report. Read the email, take its reported Sunday date from the subject and its linked attendance spreadsheet. Fall back to the known 2026 spreadsheet only when the report matches that year. Current source: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1wfc0JBM4xEMTj_g724i_ZdRoM6mvSY-_vU4MDwzxc6Y/edit.
3. Read spreadsheet metadata, resolve the actual current-year Summary tab and read a bounded A1:N range covering all campus totals, online and Grand Totals. Do not use the incomplete historical current-year tab. Preserve the raw rows, including blanks. Use all campuses actually present. The writer maps Adults, Kids, Youth, YA/YALS and recorded campus totals. If labels, columns or totals change, do not guess.
4. GET /api/attendance using the Site service credential; retain meta.asOf. POST /api/attendance using the same credential and JSON: {"asOf":"YYYY-MM-DD","expectedAsOf":"<read meta.asOf>","sourceUrl":"<verified linked Google spreadsheet URL>","reportSubject":"<email subject>","summaryRows":[["raw cell values", "..."]]}. No credentials in payloads or source. The report date must be a completed Sunday. The updater replaces only that source year and preserves all other years. It excludes future months, uses only completed reporting weeks for the current month and validates campus totals + online = grand totals. Repeating a source read on the same report date may correct source values.
5. GET /api/attendance again and verify meta.asOf, latest monthly totals, reporting-week counts, and selected campus/category values against the source. GET /api/status for concise metadata. The website’s /data.js reads the same saved object, so the page updates on load with no rebuild or republish. Do not rebuild for routine refreshes.
6. Retry only transient connector/storage failures. On stale-write 409, read current data and source again; never overwrite a newer date. If the report is unavailable, ambiguous or totals do not reconcile, leave the last verified snapshot and date intact and report the blocker in the task result. Do not send emails or contact anyone.

## Comparisons

Weekly averages divide by reporting weeks rather than calendar weeks not yet reported. For a partial month, monthly growth compares its to-date weekly average to the prior year’s full-month weekly average and is labeled. Headline year-over-year growth uses completed months only until the new month completes, while the headline attendance average includes all available reporting weeks. The prior full-month average cannot reconstruct a same-week prior-year comparison; do not imply it does.

Green >=10%; yellow >-4% and <10%; red <=-4%, using unrounded rates. Preserve these thresholds and the reporting-change notes.

## Bounded public reads
GET /api/status checks freshness. GET /api/monthly?year=2026 returns monthly rows. GET /api/detail?year=2026 returns current-year campus/category records; optional month=10 and campus=Rancho reduce the response further. Metadata appears first in /api/attendance. reportingNotes may be supplied as up to eight plain text notes (600 characters each) and appear on the website. Preserve reporting notes until the source owner resolves them.
